Suggested attribution

In a README or about page, one line is enough:

    Surname data from Chinese Naming — https://naming-cn.pages.dev/opendata (CC BY 4.0)

In an academic reference:

    Chinese Naming (2026). Chinese Surnames Open Dataset, v2.0.
    https://naming-cn.pages.dev/en/chinese-surnames-dataset (CC BY 4.0)

If you modified the data, please say so, e.g. "modified from ...".

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope and caveats

The licence covers the compilation and the prose written for it. Population ranks
and sizes derive from the Ministry of Public Security's 2020 national name report;
commanderies from Tang and Song surname books; hall names from clan genealogies and
ancestral halls. Those upstream facts are not the licensor's to license — the CC BY
4.0 grant applies to this compilation of them, and users should cite the primary
sources for the underlying figures.

Fields that are empty or null mean unknown, not zero. In particular only 30 of the
109 records carry an official national population rank, because the source publishes
ranks for the top 100 surnames only.

The full legal code of CC BY 4.0 is available at the URL above and is the
authoritative text; this file is a summary for convenience.
